    <title>Past Medical History</title>
    <text><paragraph>Historical biography with true dates. These events are not part of the synthetic care timeline.</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Historical date</th><th>History</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>February 1882</td><td>Febrile illness at 19 months, called acute congestion of the stomach and brain at the time, after which she was deaf and blind</td><td>D (CLM-0002)</td></tr><tr><td>February 1882</td><td>Cause of the 1882 illness unknown; scarlet fever, meningitis, and rubella have been proposed retrospectively (not established)</td><td>R (CLM-0003)</td></tr><tr><td>September 1911</td><td>Receipt for an artificial eye; which eye and the reason are not recorded</td><td>D (CLM-0008)</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

