<component><section><templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.17" extension="2015-08-01"/><code code="29762-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Social history Narrative"/><title>Social History</title><text><list><item>Occupation: author and advocate for people who are blind or deafblind; still writes daily, answers a large correspondence, and travels several times a year to speak for a national foundation for blind people [S]</item><item>Communication: receives language by tactile fingerspelling with the one-hand manual alphabet, her hand resting lightly on the speller&apos;s hand; speaks for herself; reads and writes braille and uses a refreshable braille display for email; reads the lips of familiar people by touch [S]</item><item>Never smoker; a glass of wine with dinner a few times a week; no other substance use; walks outdoors daily with a sighted guide [S]</item><item>Lives in her own house in the country with a long-time live-in assistant and a dog [S]</item><item>Supports: her assistant, a wide circle of friends and colleagues, and the deafblind community [S]</item></list></text></section></component>

